    {
      "seq": 25,
      "kind": "submit",
      "at": 1791660481686,
      "reason": "RegexTokenizer.train used to keep a token->chunks index and, for every merge, visited every chunk in where[p0] & where[p1]. Those sets never shrink and include chunks where the two tokens are not adjacent, so many visits were wasted merge() calls. The index is now pair->chunks (a defaultdict of sets). It is built from the initial pairs, and every pair in a rewritten chunk is added to it. Each merge pops and visits only the chunks that hold or once held that pair. A merged pair never reappears, so dropping its set is safe. Each chunk merges independently and ties are still broken by scanning the chunks in order, so the result is the same. The equivalence check found identical outputs, train_ir went down 2.96% and all tests pass."
    }
